{"id": "EUVD-2022-56064", "enisaUuid": "45b1083d-bf21-3a85-b27c-513db580a9c3", "description": "Flower before 2.2.0 contains a cross-site request forgery vulnerability because Tornado xsrf_cookies is disabled and the OAuth session cookie lacks SameSite. Attackers can lure authenticated users to malicious pages that POST to /api/worker/shutdown, /api/worker/pool/restart, or /api/task/revoke to shut down Celery workers, resize pools, and revoke tasks.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T20:55:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T13:49:48", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/mher/flower/issues/1217", "https://github.com/mher/flower/commit/a14408b16cc3d2877d36659005ce0d72b6162629", "https://github.com/mher/flower/commit/3b2115af7f9c42bd2da2fbcbd919f77013e9ec51", "https://github.com/mher/flower/blob/v2.1.0/flower/api/control.py#L25-L27", "https://github.com/mher/flower", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/flower-before-2.2.0-csrf-via-worker-and-task-control-api-endpoints"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xg8m-6cg7-cmf8", "CVE-2022-51020"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ba856cbe-1af7-34bb-a45b-381459566755", "product": {"name": "flower", "vendor": {"name": "mher"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b27c6759-e2a9-3c8d-87ec-161223559777", "vendor": {"name": "mher"}}], "isExploited": false}